    {
      "alternatives_considered": [],
      "decision": "Introduce a backend-agnostic `src/services/` layer as the sole seam between components and data sources. Service functions are async from day one so that swapping mock arrays for real network calls (REST or Supabase) requires no signature changes in consuming files. Mock data remains in `src/data/mock-data.js`; only service modules import from it.",
      "rationale": "The real backend has not been decided yet. A generic async service layer satisfies any future choice without revisiting component code. The alternative — targeting a specific backend (e.g. Supabase) now — would require re-scoping if the choice changes.",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-02T21:57:25Z",
      "type": "decision"
    },
    {
      "stage": "scope",
      "summary": "Full scope written as revision 2. Single-phase refactor: introduce a `src/services/` directory with three async service modules (searches, alerts, auth) and update the three consumers (`Searches.jsx`, `AlertHistory.jsx`, `AuthContext.jsx`) to import from services instead of mock-data directly. App behaviour is unchanged; the service layer is the seam where real backend calls will plug in later. Workflow classified as refactor/standard. Key open question flagged in Technical Notes: real backend (REST vs. Supabase) not yet decided — deferred to a follow-up task.",
